  "note": "The arrival models are causal: 'flat' holds the trailing mean of the previous arrival_window slots in every future block, 'seasonal' holds the same slot of the previous day (48 slots earlier) and falls back to the trailing mean where no day of history exists. Both spread the hold over the sites and the tightest deadline window, and hold it per block rather than per fleet. The calibrated reserve is exp018's level 0.95, fixed here rather than chosen on these weeks. The demand profile is the same single real Azure week for every arm (disclosed), and every carbon number is against that identical stream."
